{"kind":"finding","id":"F-rewind-refly-013-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RewindTreeLookupTests.cs","line":224,"method":"CanRewind_TreeBranch_ResolvesViaRoot","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.cs:5087; break CanRewind's tree resolution -> stays green because the test only calls GetRewindSaveFileName (RecordingStore.cs:5078) and asserts the branch has no direct save","what_it_asserts":"A tree branch's rewind availability resolves through the tree root's save.","why_weak":"No CanRewind code runs; the observable is identical to GetRewindSaveFileName_TreeBranch_ReturnsRootSave (line 118). The comment says the file-existence check needs KSP, but CanRewindWithResolvedSaveState (RecordingStore.cs:5103) is the testable core and is only ever called with saveExists:false in this suite.","proposed_action":"Extend to the core: assert CanRewindWithResolvedSaveState(resolvedSave, saveExists:true, out reason, isRecording:false) is true with reason==\"\" and keep the lookup assertion; then rename or split the pure-lookup duplicate.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"RecordingStore","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.cs","sut_line":5103,"case_kind":"mirror-direction","proposed_name":"CanRewindWithResolvedSaveState_ExistingSave_ReturnsTrueEmptyReason","sketch":"Assert.True(RecordingStore.CanRewindWithResolvedSaveState(\"parsek_rw_x\", saveExists: true, out var reason, isRecording: false)); Assert.Equal(\"\", reason); and the isRecording:true mirror asserting false with \"Stop recording before rewinding\".","guards":"Every CanRewindWithResolvedSaveState cell in the suite asserts false, so turning the success path into a permanent false (rewind silently unavailable) leaves all of them green.","risk":"playback"}
